# Line endings in this repository are LF - in the working tree as well.
#
# Without this, git on Windows with core.autocrlf=true converts files to
# CRLF on every checkout. That is not hypothetical: on 20 November 2026 a
# checkout rewrote both workflow files, hassfest.yaml growing by exactly one
# byte per line. The next checkout would have done the same to the Python
# and Markdown files, and nothing would have complained - no test looks at
# line endings, and git would have reported the files as unchanged.
#
# With this line the conversion is off regardless of what core.autocrlf is
# set to, on every machine, including a future contributor's.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The Apache licence text is kept exactly as published, CRLF included.
LICENSE -text
